    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature so the app satisfies the spec \u2014 *\"the request may include `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); return `salutation` = title + ' ' + lastName, or just lastName when no title is given\"* \u2014 following the existing Spring/MapStruct/OpenAPI conventions used for the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an editable `title` field to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional string) and a read-only derived `salutation` field to the `Owner` schema. These drive the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the input value survives to read time (mirroring how `displayName` is computed from stored fields).\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `salutation` mapping expression: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present (non-null/non-blank), otherwise just `lastName`. `title` itself maps automatically by name from the fields DTO onto the entity.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `title` column to the `owners` table. The test suite runs under the `hsqldb` profile.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
